#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147295 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147616 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7da19110-4b7c-547a-bd79-b4df8088678b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Polyhedron Given Its Net"}] :question/id #uuid "8bca178c-5495-5205-b213-c75b8a4df3de" :question/math-academy-id "e-2759" :question/problem "The net of which polyhedron is shown below?\n\n![](images/96/96e7889a74d2d5bd35634ec022d3c9020d23fd7292b3bd7c05f8722860389645.png)" :question/worked-solution "We fold the net along its edges to form a solid shape, as shown below.\n\n![](images/98/98ee3216b37bdce0081dd4daad1895cace7998a03d41c183184d07f6afaac126.png)\n\nAs a result, we get a triangular pyramid:\n\n![](images/32/32bdc8f811ca46a184307fa5521cb145cb0add8a0b4ee2bfae25add881561475.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147297 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147619 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fe3ef90-285d-5dfa-b540-1a6c6826ecbe" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Net of a Polyhedron"}] :question/id #uuid "4501bf84-de3a-581f-b717-10996a285921" :question/math-academy-id "e-2761" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f233556f9055563f3956eea7eaf9744fb20993084f4c3eeb5e2e35d730d8d2aa.png)\n\nWhich of the nets above is the net of a rectangular prism?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/5f/5fc1630e4e44bf68f833004ab975e406b8734fe062849484165310e093d14155.png)\n\nIf we were to fold the net above along its edges, then we'd get a rectangular prism, as shown below:\n\n![](images/c2/c2f6985ca8cd95a71409936ede80c6f257e863bd459fe5a27178a04ea3edb88c.png)\n\nNotice that the other two nets have triangular faces, so they cannot be the nets of a rectangular prism.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147300 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147620 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c8eb6c3d-6e29-59bb-af55-9dbb4be20b49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Nets That Do Not Correspond to a Particular Polyhedron"}] :question/id #uuid "1e23f3ac-bcec-5070-b135-b2285d326bc4" :question/math-academy-id "e-2766" :question/problem "![](images/84/84f39f9d765a61db544fdddc7ee79859ab4a54c2e6f0e5018512723ca0dfcfd9.png)\n\nWhich of the nets above is **not** the net of a pyramid?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/72/72462d252e84e20d567ccd10c2be12a6496f442f08d6e6baa609c5fb74f6fcc5.png)\n\nIf we were to fold the net above along its edges, then we'd get a triangular prism, as shown below:\n\n![](images/8e/8e77623f767c9cea456b787a09465397a4360915c547911a55927d8f7c9b4885.png)\n\nNotice that the other two nets give us pyramids. Therefore, the correct answer is I."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147303 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147621 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "21ee2869-b51d-5bb3-82dc-7c8d48f229b7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Given Some Polyhedra Nets"}] :question/id #uuid "1b29a574-ac81-53cf-8dd7-3030e1f9bef3" :question/math-academy-id "e-2773" :question/problem "![](images/e4/e427a98c2953792d799190b7fc20a7dbf12ce014655316e21fb809e0abc9cdc5.png)\n\nWhich of the statements is true about the solids shown above?\n\n1. The net of solid I consists of triangles only.\n2. The net of solid II consists of $4$ triangles and $2$ rectangles.\n3. The net of solid III consists of triangles only." :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the net of each solid.\n\n![](images/02/023f11b6924e6cf7318f54f5acdf910b1f688ee8ac40ec8f3b3ab7cd9c13c8df.png)\n\nNow, let's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false because the net of solid I consists of rectangles.\n- Statement II is false because the net of solid II consists of $2$ triangles and $3$ rectangles.\n- Statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147619 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fe3ef90-285d-5dfa-b540-1a6c6826ecbe" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Net of a Polyhedron"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf21374c-be77-5833-b079-b33b9eae0c0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e2/e2fdedf34ea61cf9542ebaa5c4b7bbff8ae648c3e5e4ec2a645d045469a1e1a8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145275} {:answer/id #uuid "27515621-d84d-5ea0-add3-f2c61da51deb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/74/74d7dda34e809c6833cce4ab5b234b6a2f135bcab84175ba0ec0a80520d4ae59.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145276} {:answer/id #uuid "2e80c0c8-ff46-55ab-8692-69d4eaa7ba90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d6/d6510353162c42e6609479f21719e54a67094d7acaff4295d3bf8bd772859441.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145277} {:answer/id #uuid "2fa3f056-aa8c-5a4b-b366-1bf5bec00904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c6/c603092d3d64352abf3746123afd04c58be06c56d917c6e53123fab8ea4d1d17.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145278} {:answer/id #uuid "62a41259-4d8b-5b78-a6d2-dfd5120634c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3c/3c435d5a4c009a5fd21ace2b4490e3c03b4917b939c3359de7887183f9ec6826.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145279}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3ea26da4-a51a-54ef-bf9d-5b95e05113f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145274}] :question/id #uuid "45f04d23-d77f-5812-a1db-56097793a5ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-61835" :question/problem "Which of the following is the net of a triangular pyramid?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147621 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "21ee2869-b51d-5bb3-82dc-7c8d48f229b7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Given Some Polyhedra Nets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "148d3330-6d52-5631-907b-fb5df88fab5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The net of I has one triangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145335} {:answer/id #uuid "2e11605e-4783-57fc-9634-274375ee0f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The net of III consists of $1$ rectangle and $4$ triangles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145336} {:answer/id #uuid "34b41d98-02a9-50af-b7b9-0af8b6e916d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The net of I consists of exactly $8$ squares" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145337} {:answer/id #uuid "59a72f6c-00a9-5e57-893e-f1d95b81d935" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The net of II consists of triangles only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145338} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9efeff-e4a2-58d6-9979-631509c2e7b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The net of III consists of $4$ triangles and $2$ rectangles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145339}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f2aa6e5e-3ae3-581f-b215-9e0c97daafb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145334}] :question/id #uuid "049160b7-7b99-52f8-99eb-7ab178d7e1b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-61894" :question/problem "![](images/a1/a1cb5b4cb90a334dbbd2ae44d68317680db16ff269b57f51072c7d8e965bb476.png)\n\nWhich of the statements is true about the solids depicted above?"}]}
